.SH Command palette
\f[CR]F1\f[R] or \f[CR]Alt+P\f[R] \[em] opens hed\[cq]s command picker
(same as \f[CR]:c\f[R]).
.RS
.PP
Why not \f[CR]Ctrl+Shift+P\f[R]?
Most terminals can\[cq]t deliver the Ctrl+Shift+letter combination \[em]
that\[cq]s an xterm\-protocol limitation.
The same applies to \f[CR]Ctrl+Shift+K\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl+Enter\f[R],
\f[CR]Ctrl+Tab\f[R]: where VSCode uses those, this keymap picks the
closest deliverable alternative.
.RE
.SH Notes
The plugin sets \f[CR]ed_set_modeless(1)\f[R] on init so every
\f[CR]:\f[R] command that would normally drop you into NORMAL keeps you
in INSERT.
.PP
\f[CR]Ctrl+Backspace\f[R] is bound to \f[CR]Ctrl+H\f[R] because
that\[cq]s the byte terminals send for it.
If your terminal sends \f[CR]Ctrl+H\f[R] for plain Backspace (rare,
\[lq]backarrow mode\[rq]), Backspace will delete a word at a time \[em]
rebind \f[CR]<C\-h>\f[R] in \f[CR]src/config.c\f[R] if so.
